 "docs": {
  "en": {
   "title": "Orelle tops the 72-hour snow forecast: +103 cm (16 November)",
   "description": "How much snow will the mountains gain? Our table shows the resorts with the most new snow forecast for the next 24 hours and until 19 November, in …",
   "lede": "How much snow will the mountains gain? Our table shows the resorts with the most new snow forecast for the next 24 hours and until 19 November, in Europe, Morocco and North America, with the snow line. Snow in the mountains is water held back for spring: what falls now feeds rivers and reservoirs later.",
   "sections": [
    {
     "h": "Europe and Morocco",
     "p": [
      "For Orelle (France) the forecast gives 41 cm in the next 24 hours and 103 cm in 72 hours, with a snow line close to 2,500 m. Les Grands Montets (France) should get 44 cm in the next 24 hours and 100 cm within 72 hours; the snow line sits near 2,100 m. For Courmayeur (Italy) the forecast gives 37 cm in the next 24 hours and 100 cm in 72 hours, with a snow line close to 2,300 m."
     ]
    },
    {
     "h": "Against past winters",
     "p": [
      "At about 2,780 m, Orelle has 31 cm today; a normal 16 November has 52 cm there.",
      "Only one winter in ten has more than 100 cm on this date.",
      "A week ago the same spot had 14 cm.",
      "In past winters the best snow at Orelle usually came early March / mid-March."
     ]
    },
    {
     "h": "United States",
     "p": [
      "China Peak (United States) should get 6 in (14 cm) in the next 24 hours and 34 in (86 cm) within 72 hours; the snow line sits near 5,900 ft (1,800 m). For Mammoth Mountain (United States) the forecast gives 3 in (7 cm) in the next 24 hours and 30 in (77 cm) in 72 hours, with a snow line close to 6,200 ft (1,900 m). June Mountain (United States) should get 3 in (7 cm) in the next 24 hours and 30 in (75 cm) within 72 hours; the snow line sits near 6,600 ft (2,000 m)."
     ]
    },
    {
     "h": "Canada",
     "p": [
      "For Castle (Canada) the forecast gives 3 cm in the next 24 hours and 8 cm in 72 hours, with a snow line close to 1,400 m. Pass Powderkeg ski (Canada) should get 2 cm in the next 24 hours and 7 cm within 72 hours; the snow line sits near 1,400 m. For Fortress (Canada) the forecast gives 0 cm in the next 24 hours and 6 cm in 72 hours, with a snow line close to 1,300 m."
     ]
    },
    {
     "h": "The next days in the forecast",
     "p": [
      "We place the snow line about 300 m below the forecast freezing level. Above it, the new snow stays dry; below it, wet snow or rain.",
      "Our model estimates the snow over an area; a station measures it at one point. The truth on the slope is usually in between.",
      "Forecasts a few days ahead can change: look at the map again the day before you travel."
     ]
    }
   ],
   "advice": [
    "Be on the first lift after a snowfall: by midday, sun and skiers have already changed the snow.",
    "When the freezing level rises above the resort, part of the snow melts as it falls: expect wet snow and stay near the top.",
    "Before you ski off-piste or go touring, read the official avalanche bulletin (links below).",
    "Snow on the map does not mean a resort is open: check lifts and opening dates on the resort's website.",
    "Get a powder alert in the SnowScope app to know when Orelle gets fresh snow."
